        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d07e9da7-f8cf-574c-8d8b-62bb552a0217",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Liddell, Harold Abrahams, Evelyn Aubrey Montague\n- Organizations: Achilles Club\n- Products: Chariots of Fire\n- Events: 1924 Olympics\n- Roles: athlete, rugby union international player, missionary\n- Concepts: religious beliefs, prejudice\n\nFacts:\n- Eric Henry Liddell was born on 16 January 1902 and later became a Scottish athlete, a rugby union international player, and a missionary.\n- The 1981 film Chariots of Fire tells a fact-based story about two athletes at the 1924 Olympics: Eric Liddell and Harold Abrahams.\n- In Chariots of Fire, Eric Liddell is portrayed as a devout Scottish Christian who runs for the glory of God.\n- In Chariots of Fire, Harold Abrahams is portrayed as an English Jew who runs to overcome prejudice.\n- Eric Liddell chose his religious beliefs over competing in an Olympic race held on a Sunday.\n- Evelyn Aubrey Montague was one of the founding members of the Achilles Club.\n- Evelyn Aubrey Montague is immortalized in the 1981 film Chariots of Fire.\n- Eric Henry Liddell died on 21 February 1945.",
